---
description: Evaluation and benchmarking integrity rules. Applies when running baselines (B0/B1/B2/P), ablations, computing metrics, or touching the held-out test set or thresholds.
alwaysApply: false
---
- The frozen held-out test set is never edited, resampled, or
  re-labelled to make a metric look better after the fact. If a
  labeling error is found, fix the label and note it explicitly in
  `specs/14-requirements-traceability.md` — don't silently swap it.
- Escalation thresholds are tuned only on the development split, then
  frozen before any test-set run. A change to a threshold after seeing
  test results invalidates that evaluation.
- Use `.cursor/skills/trustilo-eval-metrics` functions for every
  metric computation (Recall@k, claim-support precision/recall,
  escalation P/R/F1, calibration/Brier). Don't hand-derive the same
  formula differently in two places — B0/B1/B2/P comparisons are only
  meaningful if every baseline is scored identically.
- Every benchmark run logs cost and latency per question per stage
  (NFR8) and records its `ExperimentConfig.config_id` so a metric
  change can be attributed to a specific component swap.
- Tag every failed answer in an eval run with exactly one category
  from the error taxonomy in `specs/11-evaluation-and-baselines.md`
  — an aggregate pass rate without a failure breakdown isn't useful
  for the ablation report.
